TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION
Advertising Brochure for Eaglewood Homes

Overview

We need a print-ready brochure for our home building company. We're based in Boise, Meridian, Nampa, and Kuna, Idaho. The main goal is to get something we can use at trade shows, mail out to potential clients, and keep in the office for people who come in to ask about building.

The piece should feel professional but not cold. These are family homes, after all. We want people to look at this and think "yeah, these guys know what they're doing."

Brand Stuff

Logo
Keep it as-is on the cover (top left) and center it on the back page. Don't stretch it or change colors.

Colors
Navy blue works well as the main color - people trust it. Earth tones as secondary since we're in Idaho and that fits the landscape. A muted gold for accents here and there, nothing overwhelming. Keep backgrounds light so text is easy to read.

Fonts
Clean sans-serif for headlines, something modern but not stuffy. Body text needs to be readable - stick with standard stuff. Numbers like square footage and bedroom counts should stand out a bit but stay consistent.

Content Layout

Cover
Hero shot of one of our exteriors (Lugano works great). Company tagline. Basic contact info at the bottom. Keep it clean, don't clutter it up.

Inside Pages

Page 1 - Intro: Just a quick welcome, mention that we've been doing this for decades and care about quality. Could throw in a small team photo if there's room.

Page 2-3 - Floor Plans: Show 4-5 of our popular models with specs. Square footage, beds, baths, garage. Short description for each one highlighting what makes it special.

Page 4-5 - Communities: List the five areas we build in - Mayfield Springs, Osprey Estates, Patagonia, Shafer View Terrace, Summit Ridge. Community logos and a line or two about each place.

Page 6-7 - Photos: Pick 6-8 interior and exterior shots. Kitchens, living rooms, master suites - those are what people really look at when making decisions.

Page 8 - Why Us: Energy Star certification, warranty program, green building approach, maybe a short testimonial snippet.

Back Page
Contact stuff - address at 2490 E. Gala St., Meridian, ID 83642. Phone: 208.855.0502. Website: eaglewood.com. Email: info@eaglewood.com. License number RCE-30216 in small text at the bottom.

Print Specs

Format: A4 euro brochure when folded.
Bleed: 3mm on all edges.
Safety zone: Keep text and logo at least 5mm from trim.
Resolution: 300 DPI for print.

Images need to be high-res, at least 300 DPI at final size. Color-correct them to match the actual homes. Use the samples we grabbed from the site as reference for quality.

Files

Name things clearly - Eaglewood_Brochure_v1.pdf, Eaglewood_Brochure_v2.pdf, etc. Keep layers organized in source files.

What I Need From You

1. Print-ready PDF with 3mm bleeds
2. Source files (PSD or AI) with layers labeled
3. Fonts embedded or outlined
4. CMYK color profile
5. Low-res preview for approval
6. List of any stock images or fonts that need licensing

How This Works

We'll review digital proofs and get back to you in 2-3 business days per round. Expect up to two rounds of changes in the original quote.

Communication
Everything through email please, keeps it documented.

Project email: info@eaglewood.com

Let me know you got this and give me a rough timeline for the first draft.

















